        "code": "SUCCESS",
        "msg": [
          {
            "type": "HTML",
            "data": "<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h1>Portable Notebook and Experiment Guide</h1>\n<h2>Required setup</h2>\n<p>Change only <strong>base folder</strong> and <strong>group name</strong> in Project Settings. Use an existing project directory with this structure:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-text\">&lt;base folder&gt;/\n  data/training_data/                         # required to rerun the training/evaluation workflow\n  models/&lt;group name&gt;_lr_model/               # optional; loaded if present, fitted otherwise\n  models/&lt;group name&gt;_rf_model/               # optional; loaded if present, fitted otherwise\n  results/experiments_v1/                     # generated by this notebook\n</code></pre>\n<p>All runtime paths are derived from base folder. To reuse the selected RF, place the COMPLETE <code>group2_w2_exp06_rf_model</code> directory under <code>models/</code> and use group name <code>group2_w2_exp06</code> (without <code>_rf_model</code>). The full notebook requires the original training data; the submitted model can also be loaded independently for inference on compatible evaluation data.</p>\n<h2>Running experiments</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>On first use or after restarting the Spark interpreter, run from top to bottom.</li>\n<li>Existing models are reused with their saved parameters. Changing group name is sufficient to switch between existing experiments, even if their parameters differ.</li>\n<li>If models are absent, names ending in <code>baseline</code>, <code>exp02</code>, <code>exp03</code>, <code>exp04</code>, <code>exp05</code>, or <code>exp06</code> use the recorded experiment preset. Other NEW names expose optional parameter fields in the interface; no source-code editing is needed.</li>\n<li>In the same session with unchanged data, run Project Settings, LR, RF, Write Evaluation, Read Results, the result-name list, Chart Settings, and Experiment Comparison.</li>\n<li>Different names accumulate results. Matching result partitions are updated; existing models are never overwritten.</li>\n<li>Historical comparison and candidate-analysis paragraphs skip unavailable experiments instead of failing on a new project.</li>\n<li>Submit the complete selected model directory, this exported notebook, and the PDF report. No PDF has been written yet.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>This version preserves the assignment filters, feature selection, and h_ug/h_fg formulas. The assembler prefers original columns; creating encoders does not mean the classifier uses one-hot vectors. Historical tables below describe the completed experiments, not a guarantee about a new dataset.</p>\n\n</div>"
          }
        ]
      },
