    {
      "title": "Experiment Diagnostics | Valid Loss Counts and Feature Groups",
      "text": "%spark\n// Read-only diagnostics for every held-out experiment.\nvar diagnosticsSource = spark.read.parquet(merged_file.getAbsolutePath()).filter(functions.col(\"table_name\").endsWith(\"_indist\"))\nvar lossValidity = diagnosticsSource.groupBy(\"table_name\").agg(\n  functions.count(\"*\").as(\"test_rows\"),\n  functions.count(\"h_fg\").as(\"valid_loss_rows\"),\n  functions.sum(functions.when(functions.col(\"h_fg\").isNull, 1).otherwise(0)).as(\"null_loss_rows\"),\n  functions.avg(\"prob_p\").as(\"mean_predicted_p\"),\n  functions.avg(\"actual_p\").as(\"actual_p_rate\"),\n  functions.avg(\"prob_3\").as(\"mean_predicted_3\"),\n  functions.avg(\"actual_3\").as(\"actual_3_rate\"))\n  .orderBy(\"table_name\")\nz.show(lossValidity)\n\nvar diagnosticFeatures = Array(\"MTM_LTV\", \"CREDIT_SCORE\", \"INCENTIVE\", \"AGE\")\nvar featureGroupChecks = diagnosticFeatures.map { feature =>\n  val bins = diagnosticsSource.groupBy(\"table_name\", feature + \"_percentile\").agg(\n    functions.count(\"*\").as(\"n\"), functions.avg(\"prob_p\").as(\"pred_p\"), functions.avg(\"actual_p\").as(\"obs_p\"),\n    functions.avg(\"prob_3\").as(\"pred_3\"), functions.avg(\"actual_3\").as(\"obs_3\"))\n  bins.groupBy(\"table_name\").agg(\n    (functions.sum(functions.abs(functions.col(\"pred_p\") - functions.col(\"obs_p\")) * functions.col(\"n\")) / functions.sum(\"n\")).as(\"feature_group_mae_p\"),\n    (functions.sum(functions.abs(functions.col(\"pred_3\") - functions.col(\"obs_3\")) * functions.col(\"n\")) / functions.sum(\"n\")).as(\"feature_group_mae_3\"))\n    .withColumn(\"feature\", functions.lit(feature))\n}.reduce((a, b) => a.unionByName(b)).orderBy(\"table_name\", \"feature\")\nz.show(featureGroupChecks)\nprintln(\"Feature-group MAE is the count-weighted absolute difference between mean predicted probability and observed frequency in each percentile group. Lower is better for that diagnostic; it is not a causal effect or a probability-bin calibration metric.\")\n",
      "user": "anonymous",
      
      "progress": 0,
      "config": {
